Milestone: every Phase 0 Red baseline spec now passes. The WCAG 2.1.1 defect
that opened this track - role="slider" declared on all adapters with no
keyboard handlers anywhere in packages/ - is closed across React, Vue and
Svelte.

Parity is structural rather than maintained by hand: all three adapters route
key handling through resolveKeyAction in core, so none can drift on what a key
does, and the deliberate omission of End is enforced in one place.

The focus indicator is defined outside :where() in React so it carries normal
specificity and cannot be overridden into invisibility by an unrelated
container rule. It falls back to the Highlight system colour, so it respects OS
and user contrast settings rather than hardcoding a brand colour.

